<p data-start=3D"78" data-end=3D"213" class=3D"">Dans ce tutoriel, nous all=
ons explorer en d=C3=A9tail <strong data-start=3D"127" data-end=3D"144">Git=
 et GitHub</strong>, en commen=C3=A7ant par les bases pour aller vers des c=
oncepts avanc=C3=A9s.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"215" data-end=3D"218" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"220" data-end=3D"260" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"22=
3" data-end=3D"258">1. Introduction =C3=A0 Git et GitHub</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"262" data-end=3D"295" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"26=
6" data-end=3D"293">1.1 Qu'est-ce que Git ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"296" data-end=3D"582" class=3D"">Git est un <strong data-s=
tart=3D"307" data-end=3D"351">syst=C3=A8me de gestion de versions distribu=
=C3=A9</strong> cr=C3=A9=C3=A9 par Linus Torvalds en 2005 pour faciliter le=
 d=C3=A9veloppement du noyau Linux. Il permet de <strong data-start=3D"445"=
 data-end=3D"473">suivre les modifications</strong> apport=C3=A9es aux fich=
iers, de collaborer efficacement et de revenir =C3=A0 des versions ant=C3=
=A9rieures si n=C3=A9cessaire.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"584" data-end=3D"631" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"58=
9" data-end=3D"629">Principales fonctionnalit=C3=A9s de Git :</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"632" data-end=3D"1040">
<li data-start=3D"632" data-end=3D"701" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"634" data-end=3D"701" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"634=
" data-end=3D"658">Gestion des versions</strong> : Suivi des modifications =
sur un projet.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"702" data-end=3D"817" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"704" data-end=3D"817" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"704=
" data-end=3D"724">Travail en local</strong> : Contrairement aux autres sys=
t=C3=A8mes (ex: SVN), Git ne n=C3=A9cessite pas de serveur centralis=C3=A9.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"818" data-end=3D"918" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"820" data-end=3D"918" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"820=
" data-end=3D"847">Branchements et fusions</strong> : Permet de travailler =
sur diff=C3=A9rentes fonctionnalit=C3=A9s en parall=C3=A8le.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"919" data-end=3D"1040" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"921" data-end=3D"1040" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"92=
1" data-end=3D"947">Collaboration efficace</strong> : Plusieurs personnes p=
euvent travailler simultan=C3=A9ment sans =C3=A9craser le travail des autre=
s.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1042" data-end=3D"1045" class=3D"">
<h3 data-start=3D"1047" data-end=3D"1083" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1051" data-end=3D"1081">1.2 Qu'est-ce que GitHub ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1084" data-end=3D"1212" class=3D"">GitHub est une <strong =
data-start=3D"1099" data-end=3D"1142">plateforme d=E2=80=99h=C3=A9bergement=
 de code source</strong> bas=C3=A9e sur Git, offrant des fonctionnalit=C3=
=A9s collaboratives avanc=C3=A9es.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"1214" data-end=3D"1251" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1219" data-end=3D"1249">Pourquoi utiliser GitHub ?</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"1252" data-end=3D"1542">
<li data-start=3D"1252" data-end=3D"1301" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1254" data-end=3D"1301" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
254" data-end=3D"1284">H=C3=A9bergement de projets Git</strong> dans le clo=
ud.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1302" data-end=3D"1397" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1304" data-end=3D"1397" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
304" data-end=3D"1331">Collaboration facilit=C3=A9e</strong> avec des fonct=
ionnalit=C3=A9s comme les Pull Requests et les Issues.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1398" data-end=3D"1474" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1400" data-end=3D"1474" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
400" data-end=3D"1429">Gestion de projet avanc=C3=A9e</strong> avec GitHub =
Actions, GitHub Projects, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1475" data-end=3D"1542" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1477" data-end=3D"1542" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
477" data-end=3D"1503">Communaut=C3=A9 open-source</strong> pour contribuer=
 et partager du code.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1544" data-end=3D"1547" class=3D"">
