-end=3D"2106">git pull</code></strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2110" data-end=3D"2161" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2114" data-end=3D"2161">R=C3=A9cup=C3=A9rer les modifications avec <code da=
ta-start=3D"2149" data-end=3D"2159">git pull</code></strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2163" data-end=3D"2236" class=3D"">Lorsque vous ex=C3=A9cu=
tez la commande <code data-start=3D"2197" data-end=3D"2207">git pull</code>=
, Git effectue deux actions :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"2237" data-end=3D"2839">
<li data-start=3D"2237" data-end=3D"2574" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2240" data-end=3D"2288" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
240" data-end=3D"2286">R=C3=A9cup=C3=A9ration des changements (<code data-s=
tart=3D"2272" data-end=3D"2283">git fetch</code>)</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2292" data-end=3D"2574">
<li data-start=3D"2292" data-end=3D"2433" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2294" data-end=3D"2433" class=3D"">Git contacte le d=C3=A9=
p=C3=B4t distant (par d=C3=A9faut, <code data-start=3D"2337" data-end=3D"23=
45">origin</code>) pour v=C3=A9rifier les commits qui n'ont pas encore =C3=
=A9t=C3=A9 t=C3=A9l=C3=A9charg=C3=A9s dans votre d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t local.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2437" data-end=3D"2574" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2439" data-end=3D"2574" class=3D"">Les commits distants so=
nt stock=C3=A9s dans des branches distantes sp=C3=A9ciales, comme <code dat=
a-start=3D"2518" data-end=3D"2531">origin/main</code>, qui repr=C3=A9senten=
t l'=C3=A9tat du d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t distant.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2575" data-end=3D"2839" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2578" data-end=3D"2620" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
578" data-end=3D"2618">Fusion des changements (<code data-start=3D"2604" da=
ta-end=3D"2615">git merge</code>)</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2624" data-end=3D"2839">
<li data-start=3D"2624" data-end=3D"2695" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2626" data-end=3D"2695" class=3D"">Git fusionne ensuite le=
s commits r=C3=A9cup=C3=A9r=C3=A9s dans votre branche locale.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2699" data-end=3D"2839" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2701" data-end=3D"2839" class=3D"">Si votre branche locale=
 et la branche distante ont des changements diff=C3=A9rents, Git tentera de=
 fusionner les modifications automatiquement.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"2841" data-end=3D"2858" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2845" data-end=3D"2858">Exemple :</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2859" data-end=3D"3112" class=3D"">Supposons que vous ayez=
 un d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t local avec des commits non pouss=C3=A9s et que quelqu'u=
n d'autre ait pouss=C3=A9 de nouveaux commits sur GitHub. Lorsque vous ex=
=C3=A9cutez <code data-start=3D"3017" data-end=3D"3027">git pull</code>, Gi=
t va t=C3=A9l=C3=A9charger ces nouveaux commits et les fusionner avec votre=
 branche locale.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3114" data-end=3D"3117" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"3119" data-end=3D"3162" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3122" data-end=3D"3162">4. R=C3=A9solution des conflits de fusion</strong><=
/h2>
<p data-start=3D"3164" data-end=3D"3444" class=3D"">Lors de l'utilisation d=
e <code data-start=3D"3189" data-end=3D"3199">git pull</code>, des conflits=
 peuvent survenir si les m=C3=AAmes lignes de code ont =C3=A9t=C3=A9 modifi=
=C3=A9es dans le d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t distant et dans votre d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t loca=
l. Git essaie de r=C3=A9soudre automatiquement ces conflits, mais parfois i=
l est n=C3=A9cessaire que vous interveniez manuellement.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3446" data-end=3D"3487" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3450" data-end=3D"3485">=C3=89tapes pour r=C3=A9soudre un conflit</strong> =
