<h3 data-start=3D"2564" data-end=3D"2609" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2568" data-end=3D"2609">2.2. Explication d=C3=A9taill=C3=A9e du fichier</st=
rong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2611" data-end=3D"3795">
<li data-start=3D"2611" data-end=3D"2788" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2613" data-end=3D"2788" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
613" data-end=3D"2621">name</strong> : Le nom du workflow. Dans cet exemple=
, nous avons utilis=C3=A9 <code data-start=3D"2681" data-end=3D"2693">Node.=
js CI</code> pour indiquer qu'il s'agit d'un workflow pour l'int=C3=A9grati=
on continue (CI) d'un projet Node.js.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2792" data-end=3D"3018" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2794" data-end=3D"3018" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
794" data-end=3D"2800">on</strong> : Sp=C3=A9cifie les =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements=
 qui vont d=C3=A9clencher le workflow. Ici, nous avons utilis=C3=A9 l'=C3=
=A9v=C3=A9nement <code data-start=3D"2896" data-end=3D"2902">push</code> su=
r la branche <code data-start=3D"2918" data-end=3D"2924">main</code> (cela =
signifie que chaque fois qu'un commit est pouss=C3=A9 vers <code data-start=
=3D"2985" data-end=3D"2991">main</code>, le workflow s'ex=C3=A9cutera).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3022" data-end=3D"3116" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3024" data-end=3D"3116" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
024" data-end=3D"3032">jobs</strong> : D=C3=A9clare un job nomm=C3=A9 <code=
 data-start=3D"3056" data-end=3D"3063">build</code>. Un job repr=C3=A9sente=
 un ensemble d'actions =C3=A0 ex=C3=A9cuter.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3118" data-end=3D"3303" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3120" data-end=3D"3303" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
120" data-end=3D"3131">runs-on</strong> : Indique le type d'environnement s=
ur lequel le job sera ex=C3=A9cut=C3=A9. Ici, nous avons choisi un runner <=
strong data-start=3D"3231" data-end=3D"3241">Ubuntu</strong>, mais vous pou=
vez aussi choisir des runners Windows ou macOS.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3305" data-end=3D"3795" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3307" data-end=3D"3407" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
307" data-end=3D"3316">steps</strong> : D=C3=A9clare les =C3=A9tapes =C3=A0=
 ex=C3=A9cuter dans ce job. Dans notre exemple, il y a plusieurs =C3=A9tape=
s :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3410" data-end=3D"3795">
<li data-start=3D"3410" data-end=3D"3515" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3412" data-end=3D"3515" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
412" data-end=3D"3429">Checkout code</strong> : Cette =C3=A9tape utilise l'=
action <code data-start=3D"3461" data-end=3D"3482">actions/checkout@v2</cod=
e> pour r=C3=A9cup=C3=A9rer le code du d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3518" data-end=3D"3624" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3520" data-end=3D"3624" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
520" data-end=3D"3538">Set up Node.js</strong> : Configure Node.js avec la =
version 14 en utilisant l'action <code data-start=3D"3600" data-end=3D"3623=
">actions/setup-node@v2</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3627" data-end=3D"3731" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3629" data-end=3D"3731" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
629" data-end=3D"3653">Install dependencies</strong> : Ex=C3=A9cute la comm=
ande <code data-start=3D"3676" data-end=3D"3689">npm install</code> pour in=
staller les d=C3=A9pendances du projet.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3734" data-end=3D"3795" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3736" data-end=3D"3795" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
736" data-end=3D"3749">Run tests</strong> : Ex=C3=A9cute les tests unitaire=
s via <code data-start=3D"3784" data-end=3D"3794">npm test</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
