<h3 data-start=3D"5668" data-end=3D"5703" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5672" data-end=3D"5703">3.2. Explication des ajouts</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5705" data-end=3D"6140">
<li data-start=3D"5705" data-end=3D"5847" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5707" data-end=3D"5847" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
707" data-end=3D"5723">Job <code data-start=3D"5713" data-end=3D"5721">depl=
oy</code></strong> : Ce job est responsable du d=C3=A9ploiement de l'applic=
ation. Il sera ex=C3=A9cut=C3=A9 apr=C3=A8s que le job <code data-start=3D"=
5815" data-end=3D"5821">test</code> soit termin=C3=A9 avec succ=C3=A8s.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5851" data-end=3D"6013" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5853" data-end=3D"6013" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
853" data-end=3D"5870"><code data-start=3D"5855" data-end=3D"5868">needs: t=
est</code></strong> : Ce mot-cl=C3=A9 indique que le job <code data-start=
=3D"5903" data-end=3D"5911">deploy</code> d=C3=A9pend du job <code data-sta=
rt=3D"5926" data-end=3D"5932">test</code>. Cela signifie que le job <code d=
ata-start=3D"5959" data-end=3D"5967">deploy</code> ne sera ex=C3=A9cut=C3=
=A9 que si le job <code data-start=3D"5998" data-end=3D"6004">test</code> r=
=C3=A9ussit.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6015" data-end=3D"6140" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6017" data-end=3D"6140" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
017" data-end=3D"6049">=C3=89tape <code data-start=3D"6025" data-end=3D"604=
7">Deploy to production</code></strong> : Cette =C3=A9tape ex=C3=A9cute un =
script de d=C3=A9ploiement (par exemple, un script shell <code data-start=
=3D"6127" data-end=3D"6138">deploy.sh</code>).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6142" data-end=3D"6167" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6146" data-end=3D"6167">3.3. V=C3=A9rification</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6169" data-end=3D"6328" class=3D"">Comme pr=C3=A9c=C3=A9de=
mment, poussez ce fichier workflow dans votre d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t, et consultez=
 l'onglet <strong data-start=3D"6257" data-end=3D"6268">Actions</strong> su=
r GitHub pour voir l'ex=C3=A9cution des jobs dans le workflow.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"6330" data-end=3D"6333" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6335" data-end=3D"6397" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6338" data-end=3D"6397">4. Personnaliser les Triggers et Ajouter des Condit=
ions</strong></h2>
