<h3 data-start=3D"2990" data-end=3D"3030" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2994" data-end=3D"3030">3.3. Explication du fichier YAML</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3032" data-end=3D"3703">
<li data-start=3D"3032" data-end=3D"3082" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3034" data-end=3D"3082" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
034" data-end=3D"3042">name</strong> : Le nom du workflow, ici <code data-s=
tart=3D"3069" data-end=3D"3081">Node.js CI</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3083" data-end=3D"3222" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3085" data-end=3D"3222" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
085" data-end=3D"3091">on</strong> : L'=C3=A9v=C3=A9nement qui d=C3=A9clenc=
he l'ex=C3=A9cution du workflow. Ce workflow s'ex=C3=A9cute lors de <code d=
ata-start=3D"3175" data-end=3D"3181">push</code> ou <code data-start=3D"318=
5" data-end=3D"3199">pull_request</code> sur la branche <code data-start=3D=
"3215" data-end=3D"3221">main</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3223" data-end=3D"3343" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3225" data-end=3D"3343" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
225" data-end=3D"3233">jobs</strong> : Un workflow peut contenir plusieurs =
jobs. Ici, nous avons un job <code data-start=3D"3301" data-end=3D"3307">te=
st</code> qui s'ex=C3=A9cute sur un runner Ubuntu.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3344" data-end=3D"3703" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3346" data-end=3D"3455" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
346" data-end=3D"3355">steps</strong> : Chaque job contient des =C3=A9tapes=
 qui d=C3=A9finissent les actions =C3=A0 r=C3=A9aliser. Ici, les =C3=A9tape=
s incluent :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3458" data-end=3D"3703">
<li data-start=3D"3458" data-end=3D"3513" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3460" data-end=3D"3513" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
460" data-end=3D"3477">Checkout code</strong> : R=C3=A9cup=C3=A8re le code =
depuis le d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3516" data-end=3D"3573" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3518" data-end=3D"3573" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
518" data-end=3D"3536">Set up Node.js</strong> : Installe la version 14 de =
Node.js.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3576" data-end=3D"3648" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3578" data-end=3D"3648" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
578" data-end=3D"3602">Install dependencies</strong> : Installe les d=C3=A9=
pendances via <code data-start=3D"3634" data-end=3D"3647">npm install</code=
>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3651" data-end=3D"3703" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3653" data-end=3D"3703" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
653" data-end=3D"3666">Run tests</strong> : Ex=C3=A9cute les tests avec <co=
de data-start=3D"3692" data-end=3D"3702">npm test</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3705" data-end=3D"3744" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3709" data-end=3D"3744">3.4. V=C3=A9rification des r=C3=A9sultats</strong><=
/h3>
<p data-start=3D"3746" data-end=3D"3932" class=3D"">Une fois ce fichier <co=
de data-start=3D"3766" data-end=3D"3777">ci-cd.yml</code> ajout=C3=A9 =C3=
=A0 votre d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t, chaque fois que vous pousserez du code sur la br=
anche <code data-start=3D"3854" data-end=3D"3860">main</code>, ou ferez une=
 <strong data-start=3D"3875" data-end=3D"3891">pull request</strong>, GitHu=
b Actions va ex=C3=A9cuter ce workflow.</p>
<p data-start=3D"3934" data-end=3D"4143" class=3D"">Vous pouvez consulter l=
'ex=C3=A9cution du workflow dans l'onglet <strong data-start=3D"3994" data-=
end=3D"4005">Actions</strong> de votre d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t sur GitHub. Si les t=
ests =C3=A9chouent, le workflow =C3=A9chouera et vous recevrez un message d=
'erreur d=C3=A9taillant l'=C3=A9chec des tests.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4145" data-end=3D"4148" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4150" data-end=3D"4198" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4153" data-end=3D"4198">4. D=C3=A9ployer l'Application Automatiquement</str=
ong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"4200" data-end=3D"4398" class=3D"">Une fois les tests r=C3=
=A9ussis, il est important de d=C3=A9ployer automatiquement l'application d=
ans l'environnement de production. Nous allons maintenant ajouter un job de=
 d=C3=A9ploiement au workflow existant.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4400" data-end=3D"4442" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4404" data-end=3D"4442">4.1. D=C3=A9ployer sur Heroku (Exemple)</strong></h=
3>
<p data-start=3D"4444" data-end=3D"4610" class=3D"">Supposons que nous voul=
ons d=C3=A9ployer l'application sur <strong data-start=3D"4498" data-end=3D=
"4508">Heroku</strong> apr=C3=A8s chaque r=C3=A9ussite des tests. Pour ce f=
aire, nous devons utiliser l'action GitHub d=C3=A9di=C3=A9e =C3=A0 Heroku.<=
/p>
