ss=3D"markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light"><h1 data-s=
tart=3D"0" data-end=3D"103" class=3D"">Tutoriel Complet et Approfondi : Sui=
vi de l'Avancement des Projets avec le Kanban sur GitHub Projects</h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"105" data-end=3D"120" class=3D"">Introduction</h2>
<p data-start=3D"122" data-end=3D"560" class=3D"">GitHub Projects, un outil=
 de gestion de projet int=C3=A9gr=C3=A9 =C3=A0 GitHub, utilise la m=C3=A9th=
ode <strong data-start=3D"206" data-end=3D"216">Kanban</strong> pour organi=
ser et suivre les progr=C3=A8s d'un projet. Cette m=C3=A9thode visuelle per=
met de suivre l'avancement des t=C3=A2ches et de mieux organiser le flux de=
 travail au sein de l'=C3=A9quipe. Dans ce tutoriel, nous aborderons commen=
t utiliser GitHub Projects pour suivre efficacement l'avancement de vos pro=
jets, g=C3=A9rer les t=C3=A2ches et am=C3=A9liorer la productivit=C3=A9.</p=
>
<h3 data-start=3D"562" data-end=3D"592" class=3D"">Objectifs de ce tutoriel=
 :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"593" data-end=3D"983">
<li data-start=3D"593" data-end=3D"666" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"595" data-end=3D"666" class=3D"">Comprendre le fonctionnem=
ent de GitHub Projects et son approche Kanban.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"667" data-end=3D"718" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"669" data-end=3D"718" class=3D"">Apprendre =C3=A0 cr=C3=A9=
er et configurer un projet Kanban.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"719" data-end=3D"788" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"721" data-end=3D"788" class=3D"">Suivre l=E2=80=99avanceme=
nt des t=C3=A2ches =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99aide des cartes et des colonnes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"789" data-end=3D"899" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"791" data-end=3D"899" class=3D"">Optimiser le flux de trav=
ail avec les outils de suivi de l=E2=80=99avancement (=C3=A9tiquettes, filt=
res, automatisation).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"900" data-end=3D"983" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"902" data-end=3D"983" class=3D"">Utiliser des outils pour =
am=C3=A9liorer la collaboration et la transparence du projet.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"985" data-end=3D"988" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"990" data-end=3D"1039" class=3D"">1. <strong data-start=
=3D"996" data-end=3D"1039">Comprendre le Kanban et GitHub Projects</strong>=
</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"1041" data-end=3D"1078" class=3D"">1.1 <strong data-start=
=3D"1049" data-end=3D"1078">Qu'est-ce que le Kanban ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1080" data-end=3D"1255" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"1083" data-end=3D"1093">Kanban</strong> est une m=C3=A9thode de gestion=
 visuelle des t=C3=A2ches utilis=C3=A9e pour am=C3=A9liorer l=E2=80=99effic=
acit=C3=A9 et suivre l=E2=80=99avancement des projets. Il repose sur trois =
=C3=A9l=C3=A9ments essentiels :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1256" data-end=3D"1575">
<li data-start=3D"1256" data-end=3D"1377" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1258" data-end=3D"1377" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
258" data-end=3D"1270">Colonnes</strong> : Repr=C3=A9sentent les diff=C3=A9=
rentes =C3=A9tapes ou =C3=A9tats des t=C3=A2ches (par exemple, "=C3=80 fair=
e", "En cours", "Termin=C3=A9").</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1378" data-end=3D"1467" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1380" data-end=3D"1467" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
380" data-end=3D"1390">Cartes</strong> : Repr=C3=A9sentent des t=C3=A2ches =
sp=C3=A9cifiques ou des =C3=A9l=C3=A9ments de travail =C3=A0 r=C3=A9aliser.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1468" data-end=3D"1575" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1470" data-end=3D"1575" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
470" data-end=3D"1489">Flux de travail</strong> : Le d=C3=A9placement des c=
artes entre les colonnes refl=C3=A8te l=E2=80=99=C3=A9tat actuel de chaque =
t=C3=A2che.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1577" data-end=3D"1856" class=3D"">Sur GitHub, un projet K=
anban vous permet de cr=C3=A9er un tableau visuel o=C3=B9 les t=C3=A2ches s=
ont d=C3=A9plac=C3=A9es d'une colonne =C3=A0 l'autre en fonction de leur =
=C3=A9tat. Cela permet =C3=A0 tous les membres de l=E2=80=99=C3=A9quipe de =
visualiser rapidement l=E2=80=99=C3=A9tat du projet et de savoir o=C3=B9 en=
 sont les diff=C3=A9rentes t=C3=A2ches.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1858" data-end=3D"1861" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"1863" data-end=3D"1928" class=3D"">2. <strong data-start=
=3D"1869" data-end=3D"1928">Cr=C3=A9ation et Configuration d'un Projet Kanb=
an sur GitHub</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"1930" data-end=3D"1967" class=3D"">2.1 <strong data-start=
=3D"1938" data-end=3D"1967">Acc=C3=A9der =C3=A0 GitHub Projects</strong></h=
3>
<ol data-start=3D"1968" data-end=3D"2151">
<li data-start=3D"1968" data-end=3D"2000" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1971" data-end=3D"2000" class=3D"">Allez sur votre d=C3=A9=
p=C3=B4t GitHub.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2001" data-end=3D"2076" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2004" data-end=3D"2076" class=3D"">Dans la barre de naviga=
tion du d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t, cliquez sur l'onglet <strong data-start=3D"2063" d=
ata-end=3D"2075">Projects</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2077" data-end=3D"2147" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2080" data-end=3D"2147" class=3D"">Cliquez sur le bouton <=
strong data-start=3D"2102" data-end=3D"2117">New Project</strong> pour cr=
=C3=A9er un nouveau projet.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"2152" data-end=3D"2191" class=3D"">2.2 <strong data-start=
=3D"2160" data-end=3D"2191">Configurer le Projet Kanban</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2192" data-end=3D"2364" class=3D"">Lors de la cr=C3=A9atio=
n d=E2=80=99un projet, vous pouvez choisir un mod=C3=A8le <strong data-star=
t=3D"2255" data-end=3D"2265">Kanban</strong> qui vous fournit un tableau av=
ec trois colonnes de base : <strong data-start=3D"2324" data-end=3D"2333">T=
o do</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"2335" data-end=3D"2350">In progress</s=
trong>, et <strong data-start=3D"2355" data-end=3D"2363">Done</strong>.</p>
<ol data-start=3D"2366" data-end=3D"2819">
<li data-start=3D"2366" data-end=3D"2487" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2369" data-end=3D"2487" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
369" data-end=3D"2389">Nommer le projet</strong> : Donnez un nom repr=C3=A9=
sentatif =C3=A0 votre projet (ex : "Suivi de d=C3=A9veloppement", "Gestion =
des bugs").</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2488" data-end=3D"2608" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2491" data-end=3D"2608" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
491" data-end=3D"2506">Description</strong> : Vous pouvez ajouter une descr=
iption de votre projet, pr=C3=A9cisant les objectifs ou le flux de travail.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2609" data-end=3D"2741" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2612" data-end=3D"2741" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
612" data-end=3D"2648">S=C3=A9lectionner un mod=C3=A8le de projet</strong> =
: Choisissez le mod=C3=A8le <strong data-start=3D"2672" data-end=3D"2682">K=
anban</strong> pour avoir un tableau avec des colonnes pr=C3=AAtes =C3=A0 l=
'emploi.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2742" data-end=3D"2815" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2745" data-end=3D"2815" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
745" data-end=3D"2759">Visibilit=C3=A9</strong> : Choisissez si le projet s=
era <strong data-start=3D"2791" data-end=3D"2801">public</strong> ou <stron=
g data-start=3D"2805" data-end=3D"2814">priv=C3=A9</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"2820" data-end=3D"2900" class=3D"">Une fois que vous avez =
configur=C3=A9 les param=C3=A8tres, cliquez sur <strong data-start=3D"2881"=
 data-end=3D"2899">Create Project</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2902" data-end=3D"2905" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"2907" data-end=3D"2967" class=3D"">3. <strong data-start=
=3D"2913" data-end=3D"2967">Utilisation des Colonnes pour Organiser les T=
=C3=A2ches</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"2969" data-end=3D"3246" class=3D"">Les colonnes du tableau=
 Kanban permettent de structurer l'avancement des t=C3=A2ches. Par d=C3=A9f=
aut, GitHub Projects cr=C3=A9e trois colonnes : <strong data-start=3D"3100"=
 data-end=3D"3109">To do</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"3111" data-end=3D"=
3126">In progress</strong>, et <strong data-start=3D"3131" data-end=3D"3139=
">Done</strong>. Cependant, vous pouvez personnaliser ces colonnes pour qu=
=E2=80=99elles s=E2=80=99adaptent mieux =C3=A0 votre flux de travail.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3248" data-end=3D"3289" class=3D"">3.1 <strong data-start=
=3D"3256" data-end=3D"3289">Ajouter de Nouvelles Colonnes</strong></h3>
<ol data-start=3D"3290" data-end=3D"3506">
<li data-start=3D"3290" data-end=3D"3375" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3293" data-end=3D"3375" class=3D"">Cliquez sur <strong dat=
a-start=3D"3305" data-end=3D"3321">+ Add column</strong> en haut du tableau=
 pour ajouter une nouvelle colonne.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3376" data-end=3D"3502" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3379" data-end=3D"3502" class=3D"">Nommez la colonne en fo=
nction de l=E2=80=99=C3=A9tape de travail qu=E2=80=99elle repr=C3=A9sente, =
comme "En r=C3=A9vision", "En attente", "=C3=80 tester", etc.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"3507" data-end=3D"3555" class=3D"">3.2 <strong data-start=
=3D"3515" data-end=3D"3555">R=C3=A9organiser et Renommer les Colonnes</stro=
ng></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3556" data-end=3D"3866">
<li data-start=3D"3556" data-end=3D"3633" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3558" data-end=3D"3633" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
558" data-end=3D"3582">Renommer une colonne</strong> : Cliquez sur le nom d=
e la colonne et modifiez-le.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3634" data-end=3D"3741" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3636" data-end=3D"3741" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
636" data-end=3D"3664">R=C3=A9organiser les colonnes</strong> : Cliquez et =
faites glisser une colonne pour la d=C3=A9placer =C3=A0 un autre endroit.</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3742" data-end=3D"3866" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3744" data-end=3D"3866" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
744" data-end=3D"3769">Supprimer une colonne</strong> : Cliquez sur les tro=
is points verticaux =C3=A0 c=C3=B4t=C3=A9 d'une colonne et s=C3=A9lectionne=
z <strong data-start=3D"3848" data-end=3D"3865">Delete column</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3868" data-end=3D"3900" class=3D"">3.3 <strong data-start=
=3D"3876" data-end=3D"3900">Exemples de Colonnes</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3901" data-end=3D"4221">
<li data-start=3D"3901" data-end=3D"3970" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3903" data-end=3D"3970" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
903" data-end=3D"3914">Backlog</strong> : Toutes les t=C3=A2ches pr=C3=A9vu=
es mais non encore commenc=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3971" data-end=3D"4023" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3973" data-end=3D"4023" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
973" data-end=3D"3984">=C3=80 faire</strong> : Les t=C3=A2ches pr=C3=AAtes =
=C3=A0 =C3=AAtre commenc=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4024" data-end=3D"4083" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4026" data-end=3D"4083" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
026" data-end=3D"4038">En cours</strong> : Les t=C3=A2ches qui sont actuell=
ement trait=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4084" data-end=3D"4174" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4086" data-end=3D"4174" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
086" data-end=3D"4098">En revue</strong> : Pour les t=C3=A2ches n=C3=A9cess=
itant une r=C3=A9vision (code review, validation, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4175" data-end=3D"4221" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4177" data-end=3D"4221" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
177" data-end=3D"4188">Termin=C3=A9</strong> : Les t=C3=A2ches qui sont com=
pl=C3=A8tes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4223" data-end=3D"4355" class=3D"">Ces colonnes peuvent =
=C3=AAtre modifi=C3=A9es en fonction de la nature de votre projet et de la =
mani=C3=A8re dont vous g=C3=A9rez votre flux de travail.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4357" data-end=3D"4360" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4362" data-end=3D"4408" class=3D"">4. <strong data-start=
=3D"4368" data-end=3D"4408">Ajouter et G=C3=A9rer des Cartes (T=C3=A2ches)<=
/strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"4410" data-end=3D"4574" class=3D"">Les <strong data-start=
=3D"4414" data-end=3D"4424">cartes</strong> repr=C3=A9sentent les t=C3=A2ch=
es que vous devez accomplir. Elles peuvent =C3=AAtre des <strong data-start=
=3D"4498" data-end=3D"4508">issues</strong>, des <strong data-start=3D"4514=
" data-end=3D"4531">pull requests</strong>, ou des <strong data-start=3D"45=
40" data-end=3D"4549">notes</strong> dans votre d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t GitHub.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4576" data-end=3D"4629" class=3D"">4.1 <strong data-start=
=3D"4584" data-end=3D"4629">Ajouter une Carte (Issue ou Pull Request)</stro=
ng></h3>
<ol data-start=3D"4630" data-end=3D"4958">
<li data-start=3D"4630" data-end=3D"4692" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4633" data-end=3D"4692" class=3D"">Ouvrez votre projet Git=
Hub et acc=C3=A9dez =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99une des colonnes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4693" data-end=3D"4748" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4696" data-end=3D"4748" class=3D"">Cliquez sur <strong dat=
a-start=3D"4708" data-end=3D"4723">+ Add cards</strong> pour ajouter des ca=
rtes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4749" data-end=3D"4841" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4752" data-end=3D"4841" class=3D"">Choisissez <strong data=
-start=3D"4763" data-end=3D"4773">Issues</strong> ou <strong data-start=3D"=
4777" data-end=3D"4794">Pull Requests</strong> si vous souhaitez ajouter un=
e carte existante.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4842" data-end=3D"4958" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4845" data-end=3D"4958" class=3D"">Si vous n'avez pas enco=
re d'issues ou de pull requests, vous pouvez en cr=C3=A9er une directement =
=C3=A0 partir du tableau.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"4960" data-end=3D"4988" class=3D"">4.2 <strong data-start=
=3D"4968" data-end=3D"4988">Ajouter une Note</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4989" data-end=3D"5096" class=3D"">Vous pouvez =C3=A9galem=
ent ajouter une <strong data-start=3D"5023" data-end=3D"5031">note</strong>=
, qui n'est pas li=C3=A9e =C3=A0 une issue ou une pull request sp=C3=A9cifi=
que :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"5097" data-end=3D"5253">
<li data-start=3D"5097" data-end=3D"5128" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5100" data-end=3D"5128" class=3D"">Cliquez sur <strong dat=
a-start=3D"5112" data-end=3D"5127">+ Add cards</strong>.</p>
</li>
