<h3 data-start=3D"5692" data-end=3D"5742" class=3D"">4.2 <strong data-start=
=3D"5700" data-end=3D"5742">Ex=C3=A9cuter les Tests dans GitHub Actions</st=
rong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5744" data-end=3D"5920" class=3D"">Le workflow GitHub Acti=
ons que nous avons configur=C3=A9 dans la section pr=C3=A9c=C3=A9dente incl=
ut d=C3=A9j=C3=A0 l'=C3=A9tape <strong data-start=3D"5843" data-end=3D"5856=
">Run tests</strong>, qui ex=C3=A9cute la commande <code data-start=3D"5882=
" data-end=3D"5892">npm test</code> pour lancer les tests Jest.</p>
<p data-start=3D"5922" data-end=3D"6079" class=3D"">Lorsque vous effectuez =
un <code data-start=3D"5948" data-end=3D"5954">push</code> sur la branche <=
code data-start=3D"5970" data-end=3D"5976">main</code>, GitHub Actions va e=
x=C3=A9cuter ce test automatiquement et vous donnera un retour sur l=E2=80=
=99=C3=A9tat de vos tests.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"6081" data-end=3D"6084" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6086" data-end=3D"6133" class=3D"">5. <strong data-start=
=3D"6092" data-end=3D"6133">Configurer le D=C3=A9ploiement Automatique</str=
ong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"6135" data-end=3D"6286" class=3D"">Le d=C3=A9ploiement peu=
t varier en fonction de l'environnement de production (Heroku, AWS, Google =
Cloud, etc.). Nous allons voir un exemple avec <strong data-start=3D"6275" =
data-end=3D"6285">Heroku</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"6288" data-end=3D"6341" class=3D"">5.1 <strong data-start=
=3D"6296" data-end=3D"6341">D=C3=A9ploiement sur Heroku via GitHub Actions<=
/strong></h3>
<ol data-start=3D"6343" data-end=3D"6824">
<li data-start=3D"6343" data-end=3D"6391" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6346" data-end=3D"6391" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
346" data-end=3D"6372">Installez l'Heroku CLI</strong> sur votre machine.</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6392" data-end=3D"6458" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6395" data-end=3D"6458" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
395" data-end=3D"6427">Cr=C3=A9ez une application Heroku</strong> et associ=
ez-la =C3=A0 votre projet.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6459" data-end=3D"6588" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6462" data-end=3D"6497" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
462" data-end=3D"6495">G=C3=A9n=C3=A9rez un token d'API Heroku</strong> :</=
p>
<ul data-start=3D"6501" data-end=3D"6588">
<li data-start=3D"6501" data-end=3D"6588" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6503" data-end=3D"6588" class=3D"">Allez dans <strong data=
-start=3D"6514" data-end=3D"6536">Settings &gt; Account</strong> dans le da=
shboard Heroku et g=C3=A9n=C3=A9rez un token d'API.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6589" data-end=3D"6824" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6592" data-end=3D"6638" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
592" data-end=3D"6636">Ajoutez les secrets =C3=A0 votre d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t Git=
Hub</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6642" data-end=3D"6824">
<li data-start=3D"6642" data-end=3D"6742" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6644" data-end=3D"6742" class=3D"">Allez dans <strong data=
-start=3D"6655" data-end=3D"6677">Settings &gt; Secrets</strong> et ajoutez=
 <code data-start=3D"6689" data-end=3D"6705">HEROKU_API_KEY</code> avec la =
valeur de votre token d'API.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6746" data-end=3D"6824" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6748" data-end=3D"6824" class=3D"">Ajoutez =C3=A9galement =
<code data-start=3D"6766" data-end=3D"6783">HEROKU_APP_NAME</code> avec le =
nom de votre application Heroku.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
